<title>USA: BPA offers 300 MW peak firm power for NW only.</title>
<headline>BPA offers 300 MW peak firm power for NW only.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) continued to offer 300 megawatts of next-day firm power during peak demand hours for delivery within the Northwest only, the agency said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Wednesday power was priced at $17.00 per megawatt hour (MWh), unchanged from Tuesday's offer.</p>
<p>BPA also offered 300 MW of non-firm power during light load hours hours ending 0100-0800 and 2300-2400 PDT at $12.00 per MWh for both Northwest and California-Oregon border (COB) sales.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau +1 213 955 6761))</p>
